<title>GERMANY: Jacobs raises German retail coffee prices.</title>
<headline>Jacobs raises German retail coffee prices.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German roaster Kraft Jacobs Suchard said on Friday it would raise its retail coffee prices by three marks per kilo from March 10.</p>
<p>Jacobs said it had been forced to pass on price rises over recent weeks on the New York commodities futures market of 30 cents to $1.80 a pound. Gains by the dollar against the mark have also added to purchasing costs, it added in a statement.  </p>
<p>Jacobs said earlier this month that it planned to raise prices by two marks effective March 10, but subsequently indicated that the increase could be more than that.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097 150</p>
